From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: vmstat: restore the hidden nr_indirectly_reclaimable slot

Upstream 7aaf77272358 ("mm: don't show nr_indirectly_reclaimable in
/proc/vmstat") kept NR_INDIRECTLY_RECLAIMABLE_BYTES in enum
node_stat_item, gave it an empty name in vmstat_text and made
vmstat_show() skip empty names. A later merge in this tree dropped both
the empty name and the skip, so from nr_kernel_misc_reclaimable on every
/proc/vmstat name showed the value of the next counter: "pswpout" read
the swap-ins (it matched the zram reads), "pgalloc_normal" the
swap-outs, "pgmajfault" was larger than "pgfault", and so on. lmkd,
Chimera (PerProcessNandswap/QuickSwap) and any tool reading /proc/vmstat
by name got the wrong counters.

Restore the empty slot and the skip.
---
diff --git a/mm/vmstat.c b/mm/vmstat.c
index 234a2e7..70a4389 100644
--- a/mm/vmstat.c
+++ b/mm/vmstat.c
@@ -1170,6 +1170,7 @@ const char * const vmstat_text[] = {
 	"zero_page_alloc_total",
 	"zero_page_alloc_prezero",
 #endif
+	"", /* nr_indirectly_reclaimable */
 	"nr_kernel_misc_reclaimable",
 	"nr_unreclaimable_pages",
 
@@ -1738,6 +1739,10 @@ static int vmstat_show(struct seq_file *m, void *arg)
 	unsigned long *l = arg;
 	unsigned long off = l - (unsigned long *)m->private;
 
+	/* Skip hidden vmstat items. */
+	if (*vmstat_text[off] == '\0')
+		return 0;
+
 	seq_puts(m, vmstat_text[off]);
 	seq_put_decimal_ull(m, " ", *l);
 	seq_putc(m, '\n');
